      "widgets_values": [
        "How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 5.00-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 2D-animated anime matching Picture 1, with the same linework, cel-shading, colors, lighting, camera angle, and framing. The adult woman shown in Picture 1 begins in the exact pose, position, clothing, hairstyle, face, and spatial relationships of Picture 1. Picture 2 is the same image and is the required ending frame. The camera holds a static shot throughout. From the still opening she performs five complete vertical sway cycles in 5.00 seconds, one cycle per second, at fast enough speed to read as fine repeated shaking rather than a single lift. Each cycle uses small amplitude: her torso rises a short distance and immediately drops, repeating without pause. Her breasts follow a half-beat later as heavy secondary motion, bouncing up on every lift and dropping with a leftover wobble — two extra smaller oscillations after each torso beat — so the chest keeps jiggling between cycles instead of settling. Clothing over her chest stretches and slackens on every bounce. Hair, hips, and limbs move only as much as needed to stay attached to the quick torso pulse. Her expression and eye direction stay as in Picture 1. After the fifth downstroke, observable differences progressively narrow — body height, breast position, leftover jiggle, fabric folds, and silhouette — until she settles into the exact pose, spacing, and composition established by Picture 2 at the end of the shot, matching Picture 1 so the last frame joins the first frame seamlessly.\n\noverall_soundscape: A steady, even indoor room tone continues at a constant level from the first frame to the last, with no build-up and no fade at either end. Soft fabric movement and faint breath stay even with the repeated sway and do not swell or cut off.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A\n"
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
